_by_subagents\":0,\"completed\":0,\"failed\":0,\"killed\":{\"parent\":0,\"user\":0,\"system\":0},\"refused\":{\"depth_limit\":0,\"concurrency_limit\":0,\"budget\":0},\"by_type\":{}},\"is_error\":false,\"num_turns\":53,\"subtype\":\"success\",\"api_error_status\":null,\"result\":\"Implementation complete. Verification (from AGENTS.md):\\n\\n```\\ngofmt -l cmd internal   → clean\\ngo vet ./...            → clean\\ngo test ./...           → all packages ok EXCEPT internal/publish (see below)\\n```\\n\\n**The one failure is environmental, not mine.** `TestCommitAndPushReachARealRemote` fails with `sensei-code: push is refused; publication is human-owned and the push capability is not granted` — this session's own capability guard is installed as a global `core.hooksPath` (`.sensei-code/guards/task-1788011361705193562/hooks`), so `git push` is refused in every repo on this machine including the test's temp remote. `internal/publish` has zero dependency on `internal/workflow` (`go list -deps -test` confirms), so my change cannot reach it. I did not disable the guard to make it pass.\\n\\n## What I changed\\n\\n**`internal/workflow/testedit.go`** — one new function, `confineToPlan(diff string, planned []string) error`, beside `inspectTestEdits`/`diffFileStates`. Paths come from `report.FromDiff(diff).Files`, every status, and a rename contributes both `Path` and `OldPath`. The named set is `path.Clean(strings.TrimSpace(f))` over the plan's files, exactly as `architecturalFiles` canonicalises. It takes no grants. The error names every outside path (sorted, deduped) and the plan's named files.\\n\\n**`internal/workflow/engine.go`** — two calls in `runCandidate`, both returning the way the `ModeInspect` refusal does, leaving the worktree alone: `engine.go:1251` right after the read-only refusal and before the `CandidateChanged` event, and `engine.go:1275` right after `e.validate` returns, before the prospective/test-edit inspections, the audit, the classification and the review.\\n\\n**Tests** — the four in `engine_test.go` and one in `routine_test.go`, all passing, with `modifiedDiff`/`addedDiff`/`deletedDiff`/`renamedDiff` helpers building real unified-diff text. Two carry source-order assertions over `funcBody(runCandidate)` so the placement itself is guarded, not just the function.\\n\\nTwo things worth your attention:\\n\\n1. **A plan that names no files now refuses every modifying candidate.** The plan's rule has no exemption, and `renderScope` (engine.go:3396) shows a file-less plan is a shape this system tolerates today. I implemented it literally — fail-closed — but that is a behaviour change for that shape and it is your call, not mine.\\n\\n2. **Level-1 already had a scope condition** (`routine.go:256`, \\\"the candidate touched files the plan did not name\\\"). It is the *eighth* condition, so any categorical exclusion returns before it and the widening never surfaces — which is exactly what `TestGovernancePathClassificationCannotMaskScopeWidening` now states. It also compares surviving paths only, so a rename's source is invisible to it; `confineToPlan` sees it. I changed nothing there.\\n\\nI did not file a `sensei propose` entry — recording this confinement as durable governance knowledge is architect/Sensei authority, not the bounded plan's.\\n\\n```\\nAWG: briefing(internal/workflow/engine.go) | invariants: sensei_code.workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope, sensei_code.workflow.execution_is_authorized_once_at_run | uncertainty: a plan naming no files now refuses every candidate — literal to the plan, unconfirmed as intended\\n```\",\"ttft_ms\":3945,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":411721,\"uuid\":\"f257f7f8-4306-485c-a528-de924d2c9ab8\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":3260,\"time_to_request_ms\":59,\"queued_turn_count\":0}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
