dation (a candidate that is inside its plan when written and outside it after validation rewrote the worktree is refused before audit or review sees it), TestOperationalTestGrantDoesNotExpandPlanScope (the check has no grant input, and a test file that would be grantable but is not named is refused), TestASuppliedPlanIsNotWidenedByTheCandidate (a candidate wider than a supplied plan is refused and the supplied plan's Digest and Files are unchanged). Test in internal/workflow/routine_test.go: TestGovernancePathClassificationCannotMaskScopeWidening (a diff touching internal/workflow/routine.go plus one unnamed path is refused by this check, which does not depend on any Level-1 classification). No other behaviour changes; no signature changes; no new files.","publication":"not_offered","review":"Accept for candidate 80c2abdbc75c. It implements both required fail-closed checks on the worker diff and on validate’s re-read diff, uses report.FromDiff including OldPath, and keeps grants out of scope confinement. Sensei’s current authoritative graph states: “Shared context explains why a change was asked for and never enlarges what may be changed”; the candidate enforces that invariant. The caller-supplied diff audit is only supplemental, but source-level review and the supplied exact-candidate validation support the verdict.","workspace":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-dave-Documents-github-com-globulario-sensei-code/0c05292b-ad66-420a-9985-54db3e81471f/scratchpad/.c3-subject-worktrees/task-1788011361705193562"}}
